DESIGN.md Template

This is especially important for you.

Tell Cursor:

> Don't just generate code. Create a detailed DESIGN.md so I can understand the system after implementation.



Use this structure:

# Project Design

## 1. Problem

What problem are we solving?

## 2. Goals

What should the system accomplish?

## 3. Non-goals

What are we deliberately not building?

## 4. User Workflow

Show a realistic example.

## 5. Architecture

Show the high-level architecture.

## 6. Components

For every component explain:

- responsibility
- input
- output
- dependencies
- why it exists

## 7. Data Model

Explain important entities and relationships.

## 8. Interfaces

Explain important abstractions.

## 9. Main Flow

Explain the happy path.

## 10. Failure Flow

Explain what happens when things fail.

## 11. Design Decisions

Explain WHY each major decision was made.

## 12. Alternatives

What other designs were considered?

## 13. SOLID / OOD

Explain where principles are used.

## 14. Performance

Explain:

- time complexity
- space complexity
- bottlenecks
- scalability

## 15. Reliability

Explain:

- timeout
- retry
- fallback
- validation
- graceful degradation

## 16. Security

Explain threats and mitigations.

## 17. Testing Strategy

Explain:

- unit tests
- integration tests
- end-to-end tests

## 18. Limitations

What can this system NOT reliably determine?

## 19. Future AI Integration

How could an LLM be added later?

## 20. Learning Notes

What should an SDE2 / AI Engineer understand after building this?


